  "intended_meaning": "Identify someone who recently used the northwest track and learn what they encountered.",
  "generation_attempt_1": "You study the muddy wheels of the waiting wagons, searching for the patterns unique to the northwest track past the crates. You then turn to the man most likely to be the driver, hoping for an answer. He shrugs, wary and reserved, before saying, \"I made the run through that track this mornin'. Nothing too odd, just the usual mud and tight paths. Some of the wagons struggled with the churned earth near the old milestone, but no trouble or sight strange enough to mention.\"\n\nHis gaze flicks to the notice board, where the warning about the missing patrol still stands. \"If you need details on that, the guard captain's office might share more—if they'll trust you.\"",
